Read this honestly: scaling leakage alone shifts the metrics only in the
third decimal place. It is a methodological defect — the test rows helped
choose the parameters used to score them — but it is not the reason the
original numbers look good. The reason is that accuracy is the wrong
metric for a 15%-positive problem. See scripts/03 and the majority-class
baseline: predicting 'no CHD' for everyone scores 84.8% accuracy.
